---
import Base from "../../../../layouts/Base.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base
  title="How this site is built"
  description="The public hub, the private content bucket, the sign-in gate, and the guardrails that keep private work out of the public build."
>
  <article class="about-page">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href={`${base}about/site/`}>About this site</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
      <span aria-current="page">How it's built</span>
    </nav>

    <p class="eyebrow">About this site</p>
    <h1>How it's built</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      One repository produces two distinct outputs: a static public site and a private layer that is
      only served after the gate has checked who is asking. Research projects publish into the
      private layer on their own schedule.
    </p>

    <figure class="diagram">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 840 340" role="img" aria-labelledby="diagram-title diagram-desc">
        <title id="diagram-title">How the public site and the private layer fit together</title>
        <desc id="diagram-desc">
          The hub repository builds a public site and, through contract validation, writes private
          content to a content bucket. Satellite and pulled sources also publish manifests to that
          bucket. A gate on Cloud Run reads Firestore for the session and access policy before it
          serves a private object to a signed-in member. Leak checks guard the public build.
        </desc>

        <defs>
          <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="currentColor" />
          </marker>
        </defs>

        <g class="boxes">
          <rect x="20" y="20" width="180" height="60" rx="8" />
          <text x="110" y="46">This repository</text>
          <text class="sub" x="110" y="66">Astro hub</text>

          <rect x="230" y="20" width="180" height="60" rx="8" />
          <text x="320" y="46">Contract validation</text>
          <text class="sub" x="320" y="66">schema · paths · source</text>

          <rect x="440" y="20" width="180" height="60" rx="8" />
          <text x="530" y="46">Content bucket</text>
          <text class="sub" x="530" y="66">private objects</text>

          <rect x="650" y="20" width="170" height="60" rx="8" />
          <text x="735" y="46">Satellites</text>
          <text class="sub" x="735" y="66">pulled sources</text>

          <rect x="20" y="140" width="180" height="60" rx="8" />
          <text x="110" y="166">Public build</text>
          <text class="sub" x="110" y="186">static</text>

          <rect x="230" y="140" width="180" height="60" rx="8" />
          <text x="320" y="166">Public origin</text>
          <text class="sub" x="320" y="186">research · CV · writing</text>

          <rect x="440" y="140" width="180" height="60" rx="8" class="gate" />
          <text x="530" y="166">Gate</text>
          <text class="sub" x="530" y="186">Cloud Run</text>

          <rect x="650" y="140" width="170" height="60" rx="8" />
          <text x="735" y="166">Signed-in member</text>
          <text class="sub" x="735" y="186">projects · calendar</text>

          <rect x="440" y="260" width="180" height="60" rx="8" />
          <text x="530" y="286">Firestore</text>
          <text class="sub" x="530" y="306">session · groups · rules</text>
        </g>

        <g class="links">
          <line x1="200" y1="50" x2="230" y2="50" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
          <line x1="410" y1="50" x2="440" y2="50" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
          <line x1="650" y1="50" x2="620" y2="50" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
          <line x1="530" y1="80" x2="530" y2="140" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
          <line x1="110" y1="80" x2="110" y2="140" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
          <line x1="200" y1="170" x2="230" y2="170" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
          <line x1="620" y1="170" x2="650" y2="170" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
          <line x1="530" y1="260" x2="530" y2="200" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
        </g>

        <g class="guardrails">
          <rect x="20" y="260" width="390" height="60" rx="8" />
          <text x="215" y="286">Public guardrails</text>
          <text class="sub" x="215" y="306">leak check · allowlist · private-link check</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>
        Private content never enters the public output. The same repository builds both sides, but
        only the gate can serve the private objects.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section>
      <h2>The hub</h2>
      <p>
        The hub is a static Astro site. One build produces the public pages that anyone can read;
        a second build produces the private pages. The private build is uploaded to a content
        bucket rather than to the public origin, so a private route has no public object to fetch.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Satellites and pulled sources</h2>
      <p>
        Research projects do not have to live in this repository. A satellite repository publishes
        a versioned manifest and its rendered pages into the content bucket. A pulled source does
        the same for material that originates elsewhere. In both cases the manifest is validated
        before anything is uploaded, so a contract break fails the publish instead of producing a
        half-live project.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The gate</h2>
      <p>
        The gate is a small Cloud Run service. It reads the Firebase session, loads the access
        policy from Firestore, and decides whether the requested object may be served. The same
        styled not-found response is returned for a missing private page and a forbidden one, so
        the response cannot be used to discover which private paths exist.
      </p>
      <p>
        The gate also owns the owner-only Admin area. Admin is never rendered for a non-owner; the
        route is server-enforced, and every write is audited.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Guardrails</h2>
      <p>
        The public build is checked for the titles, summaries, slugs, routes and payload paths of
        every private item. A publish allowlist limits what may reach the public origin, and a
        private-link check makes sure every link in the private build resolves under the gate's
        base. The leak check has its own self-test: a deliberately injected leak must make it fail.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-page {
    max-width: 76ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.25rem 4rem;
  }

  .crumbs {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans, system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans, system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent, #861f41);
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0.3rem 0 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 2rem 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }

  p {
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .diagram {
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .diagram svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    color: var(--color-text, #241f1c);
  }

  .diagram .boxes rect {
    fill: var(--color-surface, #fff);
    stroke: var(--color-border, #d8d2cc);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .diagram .boxes rect.gate {
    stroke: var(--color-accent, #861f41);
    stroke-width: 2.5;
  }

  .diagram text {
    font-family: var(--font-sans, system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-anchor: middle;
    fill: currentColor;
  }

  .diagram text.sub {
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .diagram .links line {
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .diagram .guardrails rect {
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-dasharray: 6 5;
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-muted, #5c5550);
  }
</style>
